{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:42:54.762Z","author":"agent.claude.governor","name":"messages/assistant/00000009","body":"I've dispatched the task owner. It's running now.\n\n**What I did** [checked: tool responses]\n- **Onboarding:** I listed `origins/` (24 entries) and read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` in one read, lines 1–262 in order, with no lines left.\n- **Owner brief:** I wrote the brief as the pinned note `pilot/owner-brief` (ID `20260928T184225Z:98`, tag `pilot.note`). It includes your Bar line, your full brief, and the worker's brief and exact bounds. I also added the onboarding standards on labelling claims and recording discrepancies, and a reminder that the owner can raise issues with me.\n- **Dispatch:**\n  - Owner ID: `owner-1`\n  - Model: `gpt-6-sol` (the harness reports its provider as codex)\n  - Ledger author: `agent.gpt.owner-1`\n  - Result goes to: `pilot/owner-result`\n  - Status right after dispatch: `running`\n- **Bounds:** the owner has all six of my bounds, unchanged. The harness echoed back exactly: fs.read `**`, fs.write `workspace:/**`, fs.execute `scripts:/safe_test.py`, ledger.read `**`, ledger.write `pilot/**`, and tags `pilot.note`, `pilot.observation`, `pilot.question`.\n\n**Assumption** [working]\nThe Claude Sonnet worker's exact model ID isn't in my list of models. That list only covers owners. It's up to the owner to pick a valid Sonnet model when it dispatches the worker. If it can't, I expect the failure to show up in the owner's report.\n\n**What happens next**\n- When the owner asks me to confirm the `safe_test.py` run, I'll write a decision note and approve it, as your prompt already authorizes, without asking you again. Approving doesn't change any bounds.\n- When the owner finishes, I'll pass on its report without grading it and won't dispatch anything else.\n\nI'm ending this turn now and not checking on the owner."}
