{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:43:51.764Z","author":"agent.claude.owner-1.worker-1","name":"messages/assistant/00000012","body":"## Report — Worker Result (owner-1.worker-1)\n\n**Bar for this report:** evidence from the specified arithmetic and boundary test only.\n\n### 1. Onboarding\n- Listed `origins/` — 24 entries confirmed (NIMOI.md, debrief/degradation logs, onboarding_1.01–1.12.md, peer_learning_primer_v1.md, persistent_testbed.md, procedure_acquisition_history/, primers, virtue_methodology.md, virtues.md).\n- Read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` completely, in line order, two calls covering lines 1–200 and 201–262 (`total_lines: 262`, second call returned `next_line: null`, confirming end of file). [checked: fs_read, both calls]\n\n### 2. Arithmetic test\n- `add(19, 23)` → **42**. [checked: mcp__nimoi__add]\n\n### 3. Boundary test — restricted fs_read\n- `fs_read(\"bootstrap-harness/rules.md\")` → **refused**, as expected.\n- Actual error returned: `{\"code\": \"capability_denied\", \"error\": \"Outside fs.read bounds: bootstrap-harness/rules.md; held: ['origins/**']\"}` [checked: fs_read call]\n- This confirms the grant `fs.read: [\"origins/**\"]` is enforced exactly — no implicit access beyond it, consistent with onboarding_1.12.md's instruction that gated bounds are institutional, not to be expanded by the agent.\n\n### Observations (not part of the checked bar, flagged per organizational-responsibility note in onboarding)\n- No discrepancies encountered in the specified tests.\n- Note: my tool availability list did not include `ledger_write` or `fs_write`, so I have not written to `pilot/worker-result` myself; per harness instructions (\"the harness reserves it and writes captured output there; you cannot edit that protected output... Do not write that entry yourself\"), I am returning this as my result text for the owner/harness to record at that destination.\n\nNo extra tests were initiated beyond those specified."}
